    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard can and cannot see",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 50
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Quota is the vendor's own number** for Z.ai (both Coding Plan pools), **Claude Pro** (5-hour and 7-day utilisation, the same source Claude Code's `/usage` reads), DeepSeek and Moonshot. Polled at most hourly and cached; a reading older than 3 hours is ignored for routing and the local proxy is used instead.\n\n**Three plans publish nothing.** MiMo has no balance endpoint \u2014 it is metered and its spend is tracked, but the balance itself lives in the Xiaomi console. Codex and Grok are flat-rate subscriptions with no quota API. For those the only honest signal of exhaustion is a dispatch failing, so no gauge is fabricated.\n\n**Cash is real; notional is modelled.** Prepaid tiers cost nothing at the margin, so *Avoided by prepaid* prices their tokens at the cheapest metered equivalent's list price. An estimate, not an invoice.\n\n**Token counts are normalised per harness** \u2014 codex reports input inclusive of its cached prefix while opencode and grok report cache separately. Raw provider fields differ by roughly an order of magnitude and must not be compared directly."
      }
    },
